  "query_preview": "/Through Tuesday/...\nIssued at 250 AM MDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nFor today, will continue to see monsoon moisture moving across the \narea as the main upper level high is centered to the southeast of \nthe area.  PW's across the high terrain will be from 150% to 200% \nabove normal so expect areas of heavier rainfall during the aftn \nwith the stronger storms.  Across the plains, the low level flow \nwill be SSE with a Denver cyclone expected by aftn. Should see tstms \ndevelop along the associated convergence zone with storms moving \nslowly to the east across the plains from late aftn thru the \nevening hours. Additional storms may also develop along the I-25 \nCorridor as outflow boundaries move across from the higher \nterrain. Once again, with PW's aoa 150% of normal, expect some \nareas of heavy rainfall. SBCAPE will range from 1500-2000 j/kg \nover the plains but overall shear will be fairly weak. However, \ncan't rule out an isold marginal svr storm or two. Highs this \naftn, will remain in the upper 80's to mid 90's over nern CO.\n\nFor tonight, a weak upper level trough will move into wrn CO which \nmay allow for showers and a few tstms to continue over the higher \nterrain overnight.  Across the plains, should see a decrease in \nshower/tstm activity by midnight.\n\nOn Thu, monsoon moisture will continue over the area as the weak \nupper level trough moves across the area.  PW's are still fcst to be \nfrom 150% to 200% above normal.  Thus should see another round of \nshowers and storms across much of the area with areas of heavy \nrainfall. Highs on Thu will be in the mid 80's to lower 90's across \nthe plains.  \n\nLooking ahead to Fri and Sat, the upper level high will gradually \nbuild back into the area as monsoon moisture decreases.  As a \nresult, will see tstm activity become more sct over the higher \nterrain with only a slight chc of storms over the plains both days. \nHighs will be warmer as well, as readings rise back into the \nupper 90's to lower 100's, across the plains by Sat.\n\nFor Sun into Mon, an upper level high will extend from the Great \nBasin across Colorado.  The ECMWF and GFS are in better agreement \ntonight, with regards to whether there will be another surge of \nmonsoon moisture moving into the area. Both models now show\nmonsoon moisture affecting the area both days, especially across \nthe higher terrain. Meanwhile temperatures will remain in the \nupper 90's to lower 100's for highs across nern CO.",
